{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]All-gracious Master, [Cm]glorious God,
[Gm]Give me the words to pro[Eb]claim.
[Bb]Spread through the whole earth — [Cm]here and abroad —
The [Gm]honor of Your holy [F]name.
[Eb]Father, You give me the [Bb]choice,
But [Eb]Your grace compels me to [Bb]lift up my [F/A]voice.
[Gm7]If I was mute, [Eb]I'd still make [Bb]joyful noise [F]to the King.
[Eb]Oh, [Cm7]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Jesus, your name calms the [Cm]deepest of fears.
You [Gm]bid every sorrow to [Eb]cease.
Your [Bb]mercy is music in [Cm]this sinner's ears —
Your [Gm]love is the source of my [F]peace.
[Eb]Savior, You knew all a[Bb]long
That [Eb]you'd trade perfection for [Bb]all I'd do [F/A]wrong.
[Gm7]Lord, may my life [Eb]make a beau[Bb]tiful song [F]to the King.
[Eb]Oh, [Cm7]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Oh, for a thousand [Eb]tongues to sing my [Bb]great Redeemer's [F]praise!
Sing of the glories [Eb]of my King; the [Bb]triumph of His [F]grace!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Jesus you've broken the [Cm]power of sin.
Your [Gm]blood sets the prisoners [Eb]free.
[Bb]Dying you saved us, then [Cm]rising again
Ac[Gm]complished supreme victo[Fsus4]ry!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
[F]Oh, for a thousand [Eb]tongues to sing our [Bb]great Redeemer's [F]praise!
Sing of the glories [Eb]of our King; the [Bb]triumph of His [F]grace!
Your church in heaven and [Eb]earth below, this [Bb]sacrifice we [F]bring!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Tag}
Oh, for a thou[Gsus2]sand [F]tongues to [Ebmaj7]sing.
Oh, for a thou[Gsus2]sand [F]tongues to [Ebmaj7]sing.
Oh, for a thou[Gsus2]sand [F]tongues to [Eb]sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Spirit of God, fill this [Bb]place.
[Eb]Write on our hearts songs of [Bb]mercy and [F/A]grace.
[Gm7]Oh, God, we're des[Eb]perate to give [Bb]every praise [F]to the King.
[Eb]Oh, [Gm]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!
[Eb]Oh, [Gm]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!
[Cm7]Oh, [Gm]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!
{end_of_verse}
